WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.319
If I create an AWS account, will my bill surprise me?

2
00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:06.949
That's the question in this mission.

3
00:00:06.949 --> 00:00:09.945
It takes about an hour and costs nothing.

4
00:00:09.945 --> 00:00:14.037
And you can do the first three steps without an account.

5
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:19.257
Before opening any tool, open a file and write this down.

6
00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:23.080
What do you think costs the most in a small account?

7
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.330
You can be wrong.

8
00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.344
Being wrong is what makes a good article.

9
00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.925
Now download the sample cost file.

10
00:00:30.925 --> 00:00:32.581
The data is fictional.

11
00:00:32.581 --> 00:00:36.344
Paste it into your AI assistant with this request.

12
00:00:36.344 --> 00:00:37.924
Notice the last item:

13
00:00:37.924 --> 00:00:40.106
don't give me the conclusion.

14
00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:43.267
You want questions, not an answer to copy.

15
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.070
Now check the math without AI, using this command.

16
00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:54.252
The total went from 0.92 USD to 25.63 USD.

17
00:00:54.252 --> 00:00:57.193
And look at the first line of the list.

18
00:00:57.193 --> 00:01:02.998
The biggest increase is the NAT Gateway, at 16.20 USD.

19
00:01:02.998 --> 00:01:04.808
It's not the EC2 server.

20
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:06.721
Now compare.

21
00:01:06.721 --> 00:01:08.569
Do the AI's totals match?

22
00:01:08.569 --> 00:01:12.931
Did it notice that the biggest increase is the NAT Gateway?

23
00:01:12.931 --> 00:01:16.259
Did it state a price that wasn't in the file?

24
00:01:16.259 --> 00:01:19.512
If so, ask for the source and open the link.

25
00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.843
Write it all down.

26
00:01:20.843 --> 00:01:23.800
What didn't match is your best evidence.

27
00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:29.035
If you already have an account, create a spending alert.

28
00:01:29.035 --> 00:01:35.113
The commands are in the mission and run in CloudShell, the terminal that comes in

29
00:01:35.113 --> 00:01:36.088
your browser.

30
00:01:36.088 --> 00:01:38.715
At the end, you check it like this.

31
00:01:38.715 --> 00:01:44.117
It warns you when actual spending passes 80% of US$ 5.

32
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:47.269
And when the forecast passes US$ 5.

33
00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.715
And here's the part that confuses people most.

34
00:01:51.715 --> 00:01:55.501
The alert warns you, but it doesn't block anything.

35
00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:58.396
It doesn't turn anything off by itself.

36
00:01:58.396 --> 00:02:01.068
If an email arrives, it's up to you.

37
00:02:01.068 --> 00:02:06.635
I recommend keeping this alert, because it's free and protects the account.

38
00:02:06.635 --> 00:02:10.199
The command to delete it is also in the mission.

39
00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.101
That's it, you already have an article in your hands.

40
00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:18.339
The topic is how to avoid billing surprises.

41
00:02:18.339 --> 00:02:19.958
The evidence is yours:

42
00:02:19.958 --> 00:02:25.404
the hypothesis, the AI's answer, the command output and what didn't match.

43
00:02:25.404 --> 00:02:27.392
Write it in your own words.

44
00:02:27.392 --> 00:02:28.569
AI only reviews.

45
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.515
One note before we finish.

46
00:02:31.515 --> 00:02:37.628
The voice you just heard was generated from my cloned voice, with my authorization.

47
00:02:37.628 --> 00:02:40.205
And this is an independent project.

48
00:02:40.205 --> 00:02:42.709
It is not official AWS material.
